  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Engender Health Ethiopia Phase II (2023-2028)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Engender Health Ethiopia Phase II (2023-2028)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det l&#xe5;ngsiktiga m&#xe5;let med insatsen &#xe4;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att kvinnor och unga kan delta p&#xe5; lika villkor i samh&#xe4;llet och kan ut&#xf6;va sin r&#xe4;tt att best&#xe4;mma om, n&#xe4;r och hur m&#xe5;nga barn de ska skaffa; ha r&#xe4;tt till information och tj&#xe4;nster av h&#xf6;g kvalitet relaterat till sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter (SRHR), samt r&#xe4;tt att leva fria fr&#xe5;n v&#xe5;ld och tv&#xe5;ng.
Syftet med projektet &#xe4;r att ge kvinnor och unga m&#xe4;nniskor m&#xf6;jlighet att ut&#xf6;va SRHR, s&#xe4;rskilt 1) sin r&#xe4;tt till h&#xf6;gkvalitativ och lyh&#xf6;rd SRHR- och GBV-information och tj&#xe4;nster, 2) sin r&#xe4;tt till j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;llt och socialt inkluderande deltagande i beslutsfattande i deras samh&#xe4;llen, och 3) deras r&#xe4;tt att leva ett liv fritt fr&#xe5;n alla typer av GBV.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The long&#xad;term goal of this contribution is to ensure that women and young people participate equally in society and can exercise their right to decide if, when, and how many children to have;  right to SRHR&#xad;related information and high&#xad;quality services; and right to be free from violence and coercion.
The aim of the project is to empower women and young people to exercise their SRHR, specifically 1) their right to high&#xad;quality and responsive SRHR and GBV information and services, 2) their right to gender&#xad; equitable and socially inclusive participation in decision&#xad; making spaces in their communities, and 3) their right to live a life free from all types of GBV.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objectives of the Project are
1)Increasing rightsholders (young people and women&#xb4;s) capacity to know, claim and realize their rights, individually and collectively, for equitable gender norms and SRH.
2)Strengthening systems and duty bearers to deliver high-quality, gender- and youth responsive and socially inclusive SRHR information and services.
3)Bolstering existing accountability mechanisms and advocacy efforts to garner support and ownership over fulfilling SRHR.
4)Strengthening linkages with other rights-based and positive youth development and women&#xb4;s empowerment initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
